---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { kofiUrl, showDonate } from "../site";
---

<Base
  title="Privacy"
  description="What Visa Slot Notifier stores, how the Chrome extension uses data, and what it never asks for."
>
  <main>
    <section class="page-hero">
      <div class="wrap">
        <span class="kicker reveal">Privacy</span>
        <h1 class="reveal d1">We keep <em>very little.</em></h1>
        <p class="lede reveal d2">
          This service reports appointment dates. It is not a place to enter a visa
          application, and it never needs your visa-site login.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" style="padding-top: 0">
      <div class="wrap prose">
        <h2>What we store</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>A reported opening: post, visa class, OFC or consular, and the date.</li>
          <li>A random id for the browser that sent the report, used only to limit floods.</li>
          <li>Your Telegram chat id and the filters you choose, so we know where to send a match.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Chrome extension</h2>
        <p>
          The extension has two jobs: connect Telegram so you can set filters, and
          share dates already shown on the official scheduling site
          (usvisascheduling.com). Data is sent only over HTTPS to
          freevisaslotnotifier.com.
        </p>
        <p>On your computer it stores:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>A random install id, used only to rate-limit reports.</li>
          <li>A secret used to link this browser to your Telegram chat. The server stores only a hash of that secret.</li>
          <li>Your alert filters and whether you chose to share calendar dates.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>If you turn on sharing and open the official calendar, it sends:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Post, visa class (the one you picked in the popup), OFC or consular, and up to 10 dates.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Those dates are used only to alert people whose filters match. We do not sell
          this data, show ads from it, or use it for anything else.
        </p>
        <p>
          Disconnect Telegram in the popup to drop the link. Send
          <strong>/stop</strong> to the bot to delete your chat id and filters on the
          server. Removing the extension deletes what was stored in this browser.
        </p>

        <h2>What we never ask for</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Visa-site usernames, passwords, or security answers.</li>
          <li>Passport numbers, payment cards, or application answers.</li>
          <li>Screenshots or the contents of the scheduling page, other than the dates above.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Website visits</h2>
        <p>
          We count page views with{" "}
          <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/web-analytics/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            Cloudflare Web Analytics
          </a>
          . It does not use cookies and does not identify you. Cloudflare’s policy is on their site.
        </p>
        <h2>Telegram</h2>
        <p>
          Telegram delivers the alert. Once a chat id is stored, it is used only to send
          matching openings and to remember your filters. Send <strong>/stop</strong> to the
          bot to delete them. Telegram has its own privacy policy.
        </p>
        {
          showDonate && (
            <>
              <h2>Donations</h2>
              <p>
                Donations happen on <a href={kofiUrl}>Ko-fi</a>. We do not receive your card
                number. Ko-fi handles that payment under its own policy.
              </p>
            </>
          )
        }
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Base>
